Nope... Stormbringer and the Staff of Aesclepius drain levels if they
hit you and you aren't level drain resistant.  This attack has nothing
to do with magic cancellation, unlike vampires and other level
drainers.

> *mutters incomprehensibly*

The Cyclops and Ashikaga Takauji are among the nemeses you want to
kill before they get a chance to attack you.  However, the cyclops is
just a giant humanoid.  Like most other giants (titans excluded), he
has practically no resistances, other than what the artifact gives him
(level drain resistance and regeneration) and stoning resistance,
which all quest nemeses have.  In fact, you started with an item that
could have changed the outcome of the battle... your wand of sleep
would have given him a nice slumber, during which you could have bash
in his skull with Mjollnir.

Oh well, as they say in Nethack, die and learn.  Better luck next
time.

